  "exec_summary": "The European Union's Anti-Money Laundering Authority has published draft guidelines on ongoing monitoring under Article 26(5) of the Anti-Money Laundering Regulation, which will impact financial institutions' compliance obligations. In a related development, the Markets in Crypto-Assets regulation framework is planning to revise access rules for non-EU stablecoin issuers, affecting firms operating in the region. In Belgium, financial institutions should take note of these developments to ensure compliance with EU regulations. The AMLA guidelines and MiCA framework revisions will be key areas of focus for the compliance team to monitor and implement.",
